  {
    "download_url": "https://cxtoolshed.rbvi.ucsf.edu/download/chimeraxamyloidmodifier/2.0/1494",
    "notes": "Improved automatic layer detection. Support anti-parallel structures, and structures with non-identical layers such as NMR structures. Detector estimates the stacking direction without requiring Z-axis alignment or a manual Anti setting. It is more tolerant of flexible termini like flexible heads, linkers and tails, as long as a stable core is present.\n\nCorrect handling of chains spanning multiple layers. Now the detection supports amyloids with multi-rung β-solenoid architectures (e.g., 2RNM, 9NQD). Chain units and physical layers are reported separately.\n\nMore flexible expansion. Added compatible repeat periods such as AAAA, ABAB, and ABCABC, etc., ncluding anti-parallel expansion.\n\nSafer structure editing. Tried to be more careful on standards of PDB/CIF files (yet still not recommend to use on publishing files). Replaced text-based coordinate manipulation with structured PDB/mmCIF processing and round-trip checks. Improved handling of alternate locations, insertion codes, anisotropic displacement tensors, ligands, waters, annotated bonds, and sheet references. Invalidated source metadata is tracked internally, and unsupported edits produce explicit errors.",
